    "result_text": "All 257 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature. The codebase already had partial support (a `sharesHousehold` write-only flag that skipped the 409 household-duplicate check); I completed it so it fully satisfies the spec and assigns a stable shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner` model** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `householdId` field (`household_id` column) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema DDL** \u2014 added a `household_id` column to the `owners` table in all four schema files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`), since the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none` and loads `schema.sql`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `householdId` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and it's returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 restructured the household logic:\n   - Collect existing owners in the same household (same normalized last name + address).\n   - If a match exists and `sharesHousehold` is not true \u2192 `409 Conflict` (unchanged behavior).\n   - If a match exists and `sharesHousehold` is true \u2192 allow creation, compute a deterministic `householdId` and assign it to the new owner **and** every existing household member (persisting them), so all members share the same value.\n   - Added a `householdId(...)` helper deriving a stable identifier as the upper-cased first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(\"<lastNameKey>|<addressKey>\")` \u2014 deterministic, so every joiner gets an identical, non-blank id.\n\n5. **Mapper** \u2014 no change needed; MapStruct auto-maps `householdId` between `Owner` and `OwnerDto`.\n\nThe two feature tests (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.createOwnerHouseholdDuplicateAllowedWhenSharesHousehold` and `AcceptanceTest.coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) pass, as does the entire suite (257 tests, 0 failures).",
